// GENERATED FILE -- regenerate rather than hand-edit.
// The asm2hlsl corpus, embedded: every converted shader program (127 pixel,
// 94 vertex), with the corpus includes inlined so each text is
// self-contained. The inlining matters: the stock TRE set carries ASSEMBLY
// files at the same modules/ include paths (they belong to the asm programs
// these translations replace), and the include handler resolves TreeFile
// first, so a #include left in an embedded text would pick up the asm copy
// on a stock dataset and fail to compile.
//
// The stock retail dataset still ships 224 of its shader programs as
// Direct3D 9 assembly, and D3DCompile has no assembler, so a client built
// from this repository alone cannot draw with any of them -- ui.psh is in
// that set, so the first symptom is a black login screen. The corpus in
// client-assets is the fix when it is mounted; this table is the floor when
// it is not. Both lookups are consulted only after the mounted data has
// already failed (an untranslatable assembly program, an include the TRE
// set cannot resolve), so a mounted corpus or loose override always wins.
//
// ======================================================================

